---
title: "Coding is not the same as building a company"
description: "A green contribution graph doesn't mean the business is alive."
date: "2026-07-22"
tags:
  - building
  - founding
published: true
layout: docs
---

I can disappear into code for twelve hours and feel like I won the day. Sometimes I did. Sometimes I just avoided a hard conversation.

Building Algility forced the split. Shipping systems matters. So does sales. So does follow-up. So does killing work that doesn't compound.

If your week is 100% keyboard and 0% buyer contact, you're running an engineering hobby with invoices as a fantasy.

Write the code. Then go make sure someone cares enough to pay for it.
